<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip I, Landgrave of Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1504">1504</a>–1567</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Philip the Magnanimous</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip the Magnanimous was landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> from 1509 and a leading Protestant prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-marburg">University of Marburg</a> in 1527, the first Protestant university, and co-led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-league">Schmalkaldic League</a>. On his death in 1567 Hesse was divided among his four sons into Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>, Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a>, Hesse-Rheinfels and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse.jpg" alt="Philip I, Landgrave of Hesse" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Creator:Hans Krell (?) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Philipp_von_Hessen_(DE_WSE_M0076_2013-02_Overall).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
